<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Frankenhausen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1525">1525</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-peasants-war">German Peasants' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Frankenhausen, fought on 15 May 1525 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, was one of the decisive defeats of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-peasants-war">German Peasants' War</a>. An army of princes led by Philip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> and Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-of-saxony">George of Saxony</a> routed a peasant force inspired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-muntzer">Thomas Müntzer</a>, killing thousands. Müntzer was captured and executed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhlhausen">Mühlhausen</a> days later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-frankenhausen.jpg" alt="Battle of Frankenhausen" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Page077_Die_letzte_Bauernschlacht_bei_Frankenhausen_am_25._Mai_1525.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Luther, who feared that the rising would discredit the Gospel and overturn all order, urged the princes to crush it; as many as 100,000 people were killed, and the radical preacher Thomas Müntzer was executed after the rebels’ defeat at the <b>Battle of Frankenhausen</b> in May 1525.</blockquote><a href="/movement/protestant-reformation">Protestant Reformation · Course of Events</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1525 the radical preacher Thomas Müntzer made Mühlhausen his base, set up the Eternal League and led its men to defeat at <b>Frankenhausen</b> in the Peasants' War.</blockquote><a href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-muhlhausen">Free Imperial City of Mühlhausen</a></li></ul></section>
